1. What is SQL?

SQL (Structured Query Language) is used to communicate with a database.

For example, imagine a vehicles table:

| id | vehicle_type | speed | city    |
| -: | ------------ | ----: | ------- |
|  1 | Car          |    45 | Phoenix |
|  2 | Bike         |    30 | Austin  |
|  3 | Car          |    60 | Phoenix |
|  4 | Pedestrian   |     5 | Austin  |


"Show me all cars."
SELECT *
FROM vehicles
WHERE vehicle_type = 'Car';

Result
| id | vehicle_type | speed | city    |
| -: | ------------ | ----: | ------- |
|  1 | Car          |    45 | Phoenix |
|  3 | Car          |    60 | Phoenix |


